# SABOTAGE: two plausible depreciation-run shortcuts — the sweep drops its
# exactly-once read ("the unique index is the belt") and a disposal stops
# nothing (the retired asset keeps depreciating).
#
# WS-ACCT Phase 8 (ADR-054 D9) posts one slice per {asset, period}, and that
# guarantee has two layers. The caller-facing no-op is the run's
# `already_posted?` read; the table's unique index is the belt. Removing the
# read leaves the belt to refuse the duplicate — the sweep then FAILS LOUDLY
# instead of skipping, so a retried cron becomes a dead-letter storm for a month
# that is already correct. Every number stays exact; only the retry contract
# breaks, which is why the exactly-once test (not the arithmetic or the audit)
# reds.
#
# The disposal leg is the same shape: `AssetSchedule.stopped?/2` is a POLICY
# the run applies, while `slice_amount` is the contract's arithmetic. Dropping
# the check keeps every entry balanced and every slice exact — the retired asset
# simply keeps posting into months nobody reviews. Only the disposal test sees
# it, because the register and the audit have no way to know the posting was
# unwanted.
#
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/finance_assets_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: a second run in the same period is a clean no-op; the anchor is append-only
# MUST_FAIL: a disposal stops the schedule from its month and leaves the past posted
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/finance/depreciation_run.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/finance/depreciation_run.ex
@@ -154,9 +154,6 @@
 
         {:skip, reason}
 
-      AssetSchedule.stopped?(asset, period) ->
-        {:skip, :disposed}
-
       true ->
         {:post, AssetSchedule.slice_amount(asset, period)}
     end
@@ -169,39 +166,22 @@
   # ── posting ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 
